WEBVTT

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:32.980
<b>Episode 8: 
The Day of Dad's Departure</b>

00:01:37.550 --> 00:01:38.990
Yajiro.

00:01:39.490 --> 00:01:41.120
Oh, Big Brother.

00:01:41.550 --> 00:01:46.370
That's quite the grouchy voice. 
You have something to lecture me about?

00:01:46.850 --> 00:01:49.800
I'm not confident I can live 
up to your expectations.

00:01:50.220 --> 00:01:53.200
'Cause in any case, I'm a frog.

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:54.630
Yajiro.

00:01:54.940 --> 00:01:59.470
I have a clear memory of the 
last time I saw Father.

00:02:00.190 --> 00:02:05.240
That day I had gone out with 
him to visit the elders.

00:02:05.870 --> 00:02:09.730
After that, he said he had 
an important appointment,

00:02:10.240 --> 00:02:13.110
so he told me to go home ahead of him.

00:02:13.320 --> 00:02:18.240
It wasn't a rare thing. 
Father was always so busy.

00:02:18.870 --> 00:02:22.240
He accompanied me as far as Higashioji

00:02:22.240 --> 00:02:25.130
and saw me off as I got on the bus.

00:02:26.240 --> 00:02:29.110
Even now, I can remember the way he looked.

00:02:29.770 --> 00:02:35.380
Because that was the last time I saw him.

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:37.380
Big Brother...

00:02:38.380 --> 00:02:40.400
What I want to ask you is,

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:45.720
where and when was the 
last time you saw Father?

00:02:48.430 --> 00:02:54.250
Were you drinking with him that night?

00:02:54.900 --> 00:02:58.360
Did you get drunk? What about him?

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:03.530
Did you leave Father drunk on his own?

00:03:04.340 --> 00:03:06.030
Please tell me that's not how it was.

00:03:11.240 --> 00:03:13.880
Big Brother, that's exactly what happened.

00:03:15.060 --> 00:03:17.840
I'm the one who sent Father to his death.

00:03:19.840 --> 00:03:21.920
How can that be?

00:03:24.750 --> 00:03:26.820
You idiot!

00:03:37.970 --> 00:03:42.130
I was renowned throughout Kyoto as the tanuki

00:03:42.130 --> 00:03:43.930
with the least motivation.

00:03:45.850 --> 00:03:49.290
Never paid any respect by anyone,

00:03:49.640 --> 00:03:52.880
I lazed around like a Daruma, 
being totally useless,

00:03:52.880 --> 00:03:55.510
and the only time I displayed 
the will to do anything was

00:03:56.580 --> 00:03:58.630
when drinking.

00:04:00.350 --> 00:04:03.880
Father's "important appointment" that day was

00:04:04.380 --> 00:04:06.640
a secret consultation with me.

00:04:09.380 --> 00:04:13.990
At the time, I had a really 
troublesome problem on my hands.

00:04:15.160 --> 00:04:19.860
I was greatly tormented, and 
opened up to Father about those feelings

00:04:20.160 --> 00:04:21.970
to get his advice.

00:04:24.220 --> 00:04:28.230
I was in impossible love.

00:04:29.120 --> 00:04:32.140
Why was it impossible? Well,

00:04:32.610 --> 00:04:37.030
the tanuki I loved was still awfully young

00:04:37.280 --> 00:04:39.760
and on top of that, she had a fiancé.

00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:46.990
And that fiancé was my own 
little brother, Yasaburo.

00:04:48.210 --> 00:04:51.480
Yeah, the one I fell in love with was

00:04:50.510 --> 00:04:54.020
<b>...betroth Ebisugawa Kaisei to Shimogamo Yasaburo</b>

00:04:51.790 --> 00:04:53.600
Ebisugawa Kaisei.

00:04:54.370 --> 00:04:58.600
I had told Dad repeatedly that I wanted 
to part with the family and leave Kyoto.

00:04:59.200 --> 00:05:01.770
But he was against it that day, too.

00:05:02.850 --> 00:05:05.900
Our dad, who managed to trick even a tengu,

00:05:05.900 --> 00:05:09.330
had nothing in this world to be afraid of.

00:05:09.880 --> 00:05:15.340
That's what I thought, but 
even he had one thing he feared:

00:05:16.120 --> 00:05:24.090
that his sons would scatter 
or hate each other.

00:05:25.060 --> 00:05:28.350
It was Dad's earnest wish 
that we would not end up like

00:05:28.350 --> 00:05:31.260
him and his younger brother, Ebisugawa Soun,

00:05:31.730 --> 00:05:34.760
who unfortunately detested each other.

00:05:38.770 --> 00:05:42.880
I split my blood between the four of you.

00:05:42.880 --> 00:05:45.860
So it won't do for anyone to be missing.

00:05:46.570 --> 00:05:49.540
People may say the most terrible things about you,

00:05:49.540 --> 00:05:52.620
but you maintain the equilibrium.

00:05:53.450 --> 00:05:57.000
You're one of the four balanced weights of the Shimogamo family.

00:05:57.620 --> 00:06:01.210
Anyone who doesn't understand that 
isn't worth giving the time of day.

00:06:02.040 --> 00:06:04.590
You can't move away from your brothers.

00:06:04.800 --> 00:06:06.550
But Father,

00:06:09.720 --> 00:06:13.880
does that mean I have 
no option but to endure this?

00:06:19.470 --> 00:06:21.280
I'll try to do something.

00:06:21.930 --> 00:06:24.580
I don't know if it'll work or not,

00:06:24.580 --> 00:06:27.070
but for the time being, 
leave everything to me.

00:06:28.280 --> 00:06:30.760
Be patient for a bit.

00:06:38.170 --> 00:06:44.880
Then Father and I decided to 
forget our worries, and just drink a ton.

00:06:53.430 --> 00:06:54.680
Let's do that thing we do!

00:07:12.080 --> 00:07:15.280
I transformed into the False 
Eizan Electric Railway

00:07:15.280 --> 00:07:17.410
that had been giving the town a good fright back then,

00:07:17.410 --> 00:07:20.800
had Father climb aboard, and 
ran through the Shijo neighborhood.

00:07:23.350 --> 00:07:28.500
Father and I had done this any number 
of times; it was our favorite game.

00:07:37.720 --> 00:07:41.120
The last time I transformed into my 
specialty, the False Eizan Electric Railway,

00:07:41.800 --> 00:07:43.860
was that night.

00:07:49.000 --> 00:07:52.570
That night, Father didn't come back.

00:07:53.660 --> 00:07:55.030
Oww.

00:08:05.700 --> 00:08:07.600
You didn't see Father?

00:08:17.980 --> 00:08:22.770
And he didn't come back the next day either.

00:08:35.840 --> 00:08:37.120
Nise-emon was...

00:08:39.180 --> 00:08:41.760
eaten by the Friday Fellows!

00:08:49.460 --> 00:08:54.700
Because Father was drunk 
and I deserted him downtown

00:08:55.450 --> 00:08:58.550
he fell into the hands of the Friday Fellows.

00:09:11.340 --> 00:09:12.570
Yajiro!

00:09:25.150 --> 00:09:26.290
Big Brother.

00:09:28.080 --> 00:09:30.920
Even just breathing is a pain.

00:09:33.660 --> 00:09:35.800
That's enough!

00:09:42.800 --> 00:09:46.950
Swimming is also a hassle.

00:09:49.360 --> 00:09:52.050
I killed Father.

00:09:53.190 --> 00:09:56.550
It was just as everyone 
had mercilessly said all this time.

00:09:57.540 --> 00:10:00.430
I was an absolute failure of a tanuki.

00:10:01.310 --> 00:10:05.970
Rather than just being useless, 
I ended up causing irreparable damage.

00:10:07.180 --> 00:10:10.350
How could I tell that to 
everyone as you were grieving?

00:10:11.270 --> 00:10:14.420
At the same time, I couldn't 
just act like nothing happened

00:10:14.420 --> 00:10:17.230
and live with the family.

00:10:20.270 --> 00:10:26.530
That's why I decided to lock everything 
up inside and become a frog in a well.

00:10:28.050 --> 00:10:30.440
I quit being a tanuki.

00:10:31.840 --> 00:10:34.080
I can't show my face to Mother;

00:10:34.600 --> 00:10:37.940
I no longer have the right 
to call myself her son.

00:10:50.730 --> 00:10:53.460
Oh, we forgot about the professor.

00:10:54.760 --> 00:10:57.210
We have to go get him.

00:10:57.210 --> 00:11:01.220
It's okay, you can go home. I'll get him.

00:11:09.180 --> 00:11:11.940
<b>Rokudo-chinnoji Temple</b>

00:11:14.690 --> 00:11:17.360
You've neglected your master!

00:11:17.670 --> 00:11:21.100
Did you mean for me to walk home alone?!

00:11:21.990 --> 00:11:24.410
My sincerest apologies.

00:11:37.030 --> 00:11:37.840
Hm?

00:11:39.090 --> 00:11:40.920
I bet you're jealous.

00:11:41.160 --> 00:11:43.680
Kaisei brought me this gift.

00:11:44.120 --> 00:11:45.350
What was the occasion?

00:11:45.570 --> 00:11:50.000
While you were in Osaka ignoring me

00:11:50.000 --> 00:11:52.980
Kaisei often visited.

00:11:52.980 --> 00:11:57.560
And then she said, "It'll be getting 
cold soon," and gave me this.

00:11:58.140 --> 00:12:01.660
She's got a dirty mouth, 
but she's quite attentive.

00:12:01.660 --> 00:12:07.870
Doesn't matter if it's a tanuki or a human, 
you have a soft spot for any female.

00:12:07.870 --> 00:12:09.330
Shush!

00:12:11.090 --> 00:12:15.220
It's 'cause they're pretty much 
all I have left to look forward to.

00:12:37.410 --> 00:12:40.350
I killed Father.

00:12:40.610 --> 00:12:44.550
It was just as everyone had 
mercilessly said all this time.

00:12:45.550 --> 00:12:48.390
I was an absolute failure as a tanuki.

00:13:22.200 --> 00:13:23.200
Brr!

00:13:31.690 --> 00:13:33.480
Yasaburo.

00:13:34.490 --> 00:13:37.660
You're awfully quiet.

00:13:38.130 --> 00:13:41.000
I'm thinking about Dad.

00:13:41.000 --> 00:13:44.220
"Scantily clad"? Nonsense! Where?

00:13:44.480 --> 00:13:47.450
Not "clad," I'm thinking about my <i>dad</i>.

00:13:47.450 --> 00:13:50.720
Ahh, "Dad" not "clad."

00:13:53.620 --> 00:13:56.150
What about Soichiro?

00:13:56.150 --> 00:14:00.100
No matter how much you think about 
someone who's moved on to the afterlife,

00:14:00.100 --> 00:14:02.030
nothing's going to change.

00:14:02.350 --> 00:14:05.240
It just makes you an idiot.

00:14:07.190 --> 00:14:13.690
We just found out that the 
last one to see Father was Yajiro.

00:14:14.880 --> 00:14:17.330
Dad went drinking with him,

00:14:17.330 --> 00:14:20.960
got wasted, and fell into 
the hands of the humans.

00:14:21.400 --> 00:14:24.020
If I'm not mistaken, he fell into a hot pot.

00:14:24.020 --> 00:14:26.200
Well, yeah.

00:14:27.640 --> 00:14:34.720
You know, both tengu and tanuki, as long 
as we're alive, are bound to fall sometime.

00:14:35.250 --> 00:14:38.700
Even a tengu who flies 
freely through the sky,

00:14:39.090 --> 00:14:42.020
will one day fall onto the 
roof of some human's house.

00:14:42.890 --> 00:14:47.240
There's nothing strange about it just 
because the place a tanuki lands is a hot pot.

00:14:47.710 --> 00:14:52.120
Soichiro made no mistake 
about his landing place.

00:14:52.120 --> 00:14:54.620
I know that.

00:14:59.720 --> 00:15:04.890
The last person who saw 
Soichiro wasn't Yajiro.

00:15:23.900 --> 00:15:27.030
Oh, if it isn't the professor! 
Good evening.

00:15:27.440 --> 00:15:29.270
Is that Soichiro?

00:15:29.870 --> 00:15:31.860
It's chilly out, huh.

00:15:32.370 --> 00:15:33.990
Have a nip?

00:15:34.410 --> 00:15:37.570
Don't mind if I do.

00:15:41.210 --> 00:15:44.030
Why are you here as a hairball?

00:15:44.370 --> 00:15:47.880
I'm past the point where I can transform.

00:15:54.150 --> 00:15:56.440
So this is my final drink.

00:15:57.000 --> 00:16:00.680
Soichiro, are you dead?

00:16:01.430 --> 00:16:05.690
I'm afraid it seems as though 
I was just boiled in a hot pot.

00:16:10.520 --> 00:16:13.070
Of all the idiotic things to do!

00:16:13.290 --> 00:16:15.140
Oh, don't say that.

00:16:15.380 --> 00:16:17.950
It's a road everyone takes at some point.

00:16:17.950 --> 00:16:23.050
But I told you, didn't I? 
To go easy on the screwing around?

00:16:23.640 --> 00:16:26.440
At any rate, I'm a tanuki,

00:16:26.440 --> 00:16:29.590
so I can't do that so easily.

00:16:30.010 --> 00:16:34.090
This is yet another manifestation 
of my idiot blood.

00:16:37.100 --> 00:16:38.590
Professor,

00:16:38.590 --> 00:16:43.100
please continue to look after Yasaburo.

00:16:43.610 --> 00:16:45.570
He's a weird one.

00:16:46.360 --> 00:16:49.490
His idiocy resembles yours to a tee.

00:16:49.830 --> 00:16:52.610
But isn't he a bit <i>too</i> idiotic?

00:16:52.850 --> 00:16:54.380
Truly.

00:16:55.110 --> 00:16:58.790
But I expect that.

00:16:59.510 --> 00:17:04.130
I know it will cause some trouble for you, 
but whatever you can do is most appreciated.

00:17:05.120 --> 00:17:08.870
Someday I'm sure he'll make 
himself useful to you.

00:17:10.550 --> 00:17:11.880
Mm.

00:17:12.620 --> 00:17:15.430
Well, I've got to be going.

00:17:16.980 --> 00:17:18.970
Soichiro.

00:17:20.230 --> 00:17:23.720
It's a shame we have to part.

00:17:24.290 --> 00:17:26.630
Just between us, though.

00:17:28.490 --> 00:17:31.200
That's great to hear.

00:17:31.740 --> 00:17:34.120
I can take it as a souvenir to the afterlife.

00:17:47.180 --> 00:17:51.710
Well, Shimogamo Soichiro is 
retiring early. Do excuse me.

00:17:52.440 --> 00:17:55.190
There were many bothersome matters,

00:17:55.190 --> 00:17:58.120
but it was, more or less, a pleasant life.

00:17:59.140 --> 00:18:06.720
I sincerely appreciate the kindess you've 
shown me all these years, Nyoigatake Yakushibo.

00:18:17.630 --> 00:18:19.400
That happened?

00:18:19.740 --> 00:18:23.120
He was an idiot to the last.

00:18:23.780 --> 00:18:26.870
It's too bad he was a tanuki.

00:18:29.330 --> 00:18:33.130
Well, good night, Professor.

00:19:08.420 --> 00:19:09.920
Big Brother...

00:19:11.020 --> 00:19:12.560
Father...

00:19:21.570 --> 00:19:23.110
Did something happen?

00:19:23.760 --> 00:19:26.970
We were at Yajiro's place.

00:19:27.390 --> 00:19:28.980
Did you have a fight or something?

00:19:35.800 --> 00:19:37.060
Mother.

00:19:37.950 --> 00:19:42.010
About the night that 
Father didn't come home,

00:19:42.900 --> 00:19:44.320
well...

00:19:45.010 --> 00:19:48.870
You know, he was so troubled.

00:19:50.830 --> 00:19:54.960
You know, he was in love with Kaisei.

00:19:56.280 --> 00:19:57.560
Yeah.

00:19:58.070 --> 00:20:02.970
And then, he consulted with So about it.

00:20:04.350 --> 00:20:08.220
Hey, Mother is worried.

00:20:08.630 --> 00:20:09.810
Say something.

00:20:11.730 --> 00:20:13.110
Mother.

00:20:13.580 --> 00:20:14.740
What's up?

00:20:16.050 --> 00:20:18.350
You knew?

00:20:18.670 --> 00:20:20.130
Knew what?

00:20:21.240 --> 00:20:24.110
Why Yajiro holed up in a well.

00:20:28.140 --> 00:20:30.280
He's my son.

00:20:30.730 --> 00:20:35.380
If I didn't understand, 
it'd be too hard on him.

00:20:37.250 --> 00:20:38.830
So Yaichiro,

00:20:39.390 --> 00:20:43.290
please, please don't 
blame him too much.

00:20:44.120 --> 00:20:46.170
I know.

00:20:46.410 --> 00:20:49.390
I understand him very well.

00:20:50.400 --> 00:20:54.890
If you're his big brother, 
then please understand how he feels.

00:20:55.130 --> 00:20:59.900
I do, Mother. He's my little brother.

00:21:00.220 --> 00:21:01.960
I understand him, too.

00:21:02.960 --> 00:21:06.060
I understand him; that's why it hurts.

00:21:10.400 --> 00:21:12.960
When saying goodbye to this world,

00:21:13.440 --> 00:21:18.680
our father split his great blood into four:

00:21:19.670 --> 00:21:22.630
the eldest inherited only 
his sense of responsibility;

00:21:22.890 --> 00:21:26.130
the second eldest inherited 
only his easygoing personality;

00:21:26.630 --> 00:21:29.470
our little brother inherited 
only his innocence;

00:21:30.250 --> 00:21:34.330
as for me, I inherited only his idiocy.

00:21:36.710 --> 00:21:40.260
What held us diverse brothers together was

00:21:40.780 --> 00:21:43.380
the love of our mother, deeper than the sea,

00:21:44.020 --> 00:21:46.920
and parting with our great dad.

00:21:48.470 --> 00:21:50.930
One major departure

00:21:51.800 --> 00:21:55.180
can connect the ones left behind.

00:23:31.100 --> 00:23:35.350
There is something I wanted 
to ask, if Uncle were still alive.

00:23:36.030 --> 00:23:39.430
Why is my name "Kaisei"?

00:23:37.680 --> 00:23:39.920
<b>Kaisei, Daughter of Ebisugawa</b>
